# natpmpc - Network Address Translation Port Map Protocol Client
#
# This package provides a command-line utility to request port mappings
# via the NAT-PMP (RFC 6886) protocol. It is a client tool, not a daemon
# or service, so it has no persistent configuration file.
#
# Configuration, if any, is typically passed via command-line arguments
# at runtime (e.g., specifying the gateway IP, port, and protocol).
# It does not connect to external backends defined in the capability
# vocabulary (databases, caches, etc.) in a service-oriented way.

# No configuration template needed.
# The utility is invoked as: natpmpc [-s source_addr] [-d dest_addr] -p proto:port:ext_port [gateway]
# See 'man natpmpc' for usage details.